---
// About page
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TechnologyLogos from '../components/TechnologyLogos.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="About" 
  description="Technical Architect with expertise in healthcare interoperability, HL7 FHIR, and API architecture"
>
  <div class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About Me</h1>
      
      <div class="content-wrapper">
        <p class="lead">
          I'm a Technical Architect specializing in healthcare interoperability, 
          with deep expertise in HL7 FHIR, CDA, and cross-border healthcare data exchange.
        </p>
        
        <h2>Background</h2>
        <p>
          I work at the intersection of healthcare, standards, and practical software delivery. 
          I'm a full-stack web developer working as a Technical Architect, based in Clane, Ireland.
          I enjoy coding and problem-solving, but most of all, I enjoy being part of a much bigger team.
        </p>
        
        <p>
          My focus is on making complex interoperability problems understandable and building 
          systems that work reliably in production. I work with the Health Service Executive (HSE) 
          in Ireland, leading technical architecture for healthcare interoperability initiatives 
          including Ireland's implementation of MyHealth@EU for cross-border patient data exchange.
        </p>
        
        <h2>Expertise</h2>
        
        <h3>Healthcare Standards & Interoperability</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>HL7 FHIR</strong> - Implementation, profiling, and governance across healthcare systems</li>
          <li><strong>HL7 CDA</strong> - Clinical document architecture and transformation workflows</li>
          <li><strong>MyHealth@EU</strong> - Cross-border healthcare data exchange and Patient Summary</li>
          <li><strong>IHE Profiles</strong> - XDS, XCA, and other integration patterns</li>
          <li><strong>Medical Imaging</strong> - DICOM, IHE XDS-I, and imaging interoperability</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>Technical Architecture</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>API Design</strong> - RESTful APIs, governance, documentation, and developer experience</li>
          <li><strong>Integration Platforms</strong> - Design and delivery of healthcare integration infrastructure</li>
          <li><strong>Terminology Services</strong> - FHIR terminology servers, SNOMED CT, and clinical coding systems</li>
          <li><strong>Medication Management</strong> - National medicinal product catalogues and ePrescription infrastructure</li>
          <li><strong>Security Architecture</strong> - Healthcare data protection and privacy-preserving design</li>
          <li><strong>Cloud Architecture</strong> - Azure-based healthcare solutions and modern deployment patterns</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>Software Development</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Python</strong> - Django, Django REST Framework, Flask</li>
          <li><strong>Frontend</strong> - Angular, TypeScript, HTML, JavaScript</li>
          <li><strong>Java</strong> - Healthcare integration servers and tools</li>
          <li><strong>Data</strong> - PostgreSQL, MongoDB, data modeling for healthcare</li>
          <li><strong>DevOps</strong> - Docker, CI/CD, containerization</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Approach</h2>
        <p>
          I believe in:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Standards-based solutions</strong> that enable interoperability</li>
          <li><strong>Clear documentation</strong> that makes complex topics accessible</li>
          <li><strong>Practical delivery</strong> over theoretical perfection</li>
          <li><strong>Developer experience</strong> as a key success factor</li>
          <li><strong>Security and privacy</strong> by design</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <TechnologyLogos />

  <div class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Current Focus</h2>
        <p>
          My current work involves:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Leading technical architecture for Ireland's <strong>MyHealth@EU</strong> implementation as part of the European Health Data Space (EHDS)</li>
          <li>Contributing to <strong>Xt-EHR</strong> (European Health Data Space project) across multiple work packages:
            <ul>
              <li>WP6.1: Patient Summaries towards EHDS</li>
              <li>WP6.2: Electronic Prescriptions and Dispensations</li>
              <li>WP7.1: Laboratory Results and Reports</li>
              <li>WP7.2: Medical Imaging and Reports</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>Establishing FHIR as the primary integration standard for HSE systems</li>
          <li>Designing API platforms and developer tools for healthcare integration</li>
          <li>Active participation in European healthcare interoperability working groups and standards development</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>MyHealth@EU: Cross-Border Healthcare in Europe</h3>
        <p>
          Leading the technical architecture for Ireland's National Contact Point (NCP) for eHealth, 
          enabling secure cross-border exchange of healthcare data across the European Union. 
          MyHealth@EU is the operational service supporting the European Health Data Space Regulation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Current Services:</strong>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Patient Summary</strong> - Essential medical information for treatment abroad</li>
          <li><strong>ePrescription/eDispensation</strong> - Cross-border medication prescribing and dispensing</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Future Services (in development with Xt-EHR):</strong>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Laboratory results and reports</li>
          <li>Hospital discharge reports</li>
          <li>Medical images (X-rays, MRI, CT scans)</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>National Infrastructure & Standards</h3>
        <p>
          Contributing to Ireland's foundational interoperability infrastructure:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>National Medicinal Product Catalogue (NMPC)</strong> - Testing and evaluation of national medication management API using SNOMED CT terminology, supporting integrated medicine management across primary and secondary care</li>
          <li><strong>Central Terminology Server (CTS)</strong> - Evaluation of FHIR terminology service providing SNOMED CT and Irish clinical reference sets for standardized clinical data representation</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These services provide the foundational terminology and medication infrastructure that enables 
          MyHealth@EU ePrescription services and FHIR-based integration across Irish healthcare systems.
        </p>
        
        <h3>Xt-EHR Project: Building EHDS Technical Specifications</h3>
        <p>
          The Xt-EHR project develops the technical specifications and implementation guides 
          that services like MyHealth@EU implement. Contributing to multiple work packages 
          developing FHIR-based standards for:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Patient Summaries (WP6.1)</strong> - Core patient data for cross-border exchange</li>
          <li><strong>Electronic Prescriptions & Dispensations (WP6.2)</strong> - Medication workflows and safety</li>
          <li><strong>Laboratory Results (WP7.1)</strong> - Diagnostic test results using LOINC, NPU, and SNOMED CT</li>
          <li><strong>Medical Imaging Reports (WP7.2)</strong> - Radiology reports using HL7 FHIR and DICOM standards</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Certifications & Professional Development</h2>
        <p>
          Continuous learning in healthcare interoperability standards and technical architecture:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>openEHR & HL7 FHIR Technical Course</strong> - Better (openEHR & HL7 FHIR collaboration), May 2026</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Standards Development & Working Groups</h2>
        <p>
          Active participation in European and international healthcare standards development:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>HL7 Europe - Medication Prescription and Dispense Working Group</strong> - Contributing to FHIR Implementation Guide development for European exchange format (EEHRxF) under EHDS Regulation, in collaboration with IHE and European projects (XpanDH, Xt-EHR, xShare, UNICOM)</li>
          <li><strong>Xt-EHR Project Working Groups</strong> - Active contributor to WP6.1, 6.2, 7.1, and 7.2 technical specifications</li>
          <li><strong>European eHealth Network</strong> - Technical representation in EHDS implementation discussions</li>
          <li><strong>MyHealth@EU Community</strong> - Collaboration with Member States on cross-border data exchange</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Connect</h2>
        <p>
          I'm interested in healthcare interoperability challenges, standards implementation, 
          and how technology can improve healthcare delivery.
        </p>
        
        <div class="btn-group" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">
          <a href="/projects" class="btn btn-primary">View Projects</a>
          <a href="/timeline" class="btn btn-outline">See Timeline</a>
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-secondary">Get in Touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
